'''Wildmutt''' is the [[Omnitrix|Omnitrix's]] DNA sample of a [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancer]]<ref>[[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil Billings]]</ref><ref>[[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max Tennyson]]</ref><ref name="Truth">''[[Truth]]''</ref> from the planet [[Vulpin]].{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Bandai Lenticular Card.png]]|group = Bandai}}

==Appearance==
===Ben as Wildmutt===
Wildmutt appears to be a large orange dog-like creature with no eyes, ears, nose, or tail. He stands on all fours and his movements are somewhat apelike. His teeth are very defined and his bottom jaw sticks out of his mouth. The various [[wikipedia:Spine (zoology)|spines]] found all across his body function similarly to whiskers with tactile sensing, and are not fur.{{Refn|https://archive.is/wrgzq|group = DJ}} Since Wildmutt has no eyes, he uses his sense of smell and hearing to navigate, which are aided by three gill-like nostrils located on each side of his neck.

In the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''', Wildmutt wore a black-and-white brace with the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]] symbol on his left shoulder.

While under the effects of a cold in ''[[Side Effects]]'', Wildmutt's fur discolors from its vivid orange to a pale yellowish-orange tone, and his lips and claws turn from black to a sickly dark green hue.

In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Wildmutt wore a yellow raincoat.

In ''[[Merry Christmas]]'', Wildmutt briefly wore fake antlers while disguised as a reindeer.

In ''[[Don't Drink the Water]]'', 4-year-old Wildmutt, nicknamed Wildpup, looked very similar to his 10-year-old self, but a lot smaller and thinner nails instead of claws.

In '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens|Destroy All Aliens]]''''', Wildmutt's skin was lighter and his fur was more defined.

In '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time|Race Against Time]]''''', Wildmutt looks the same, except his skin is darker.

In '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', 16-year-old Wildmutt looks mostly the same except his skin is lighter in color. While his lips were still black in the '''Ultimate Alien''' [[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)/Theme Song|intro]], they were in the same color as his fur in the actual series. He wore the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] symbol on his chest. Kevin as Wildmutt shares these traits.

In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', 10-year-old Wildmutt looked mostly the same as in the '''Original Series''', except his lips were in the same color has his skin, his shoulder brace did not have any white on it, and the original Omnitrix symbol was recolored green.

In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Heroes United]]'', 16-year-old Wildmutt looked exactly the same as in the '''Original Series''' but his skin was a darkish orange.

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Wildmutt's lips have returned to being black and his forearms are a bit bigger. 16-year-old Wildmutt wears a green and white collar with the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol.

11-year-old Wildmutt looks closer to his appearance in the '''Original Series''' than 10-year-old Wildmutt in '''Ultimate Alien''', with the white returning to the shoulder brace, though the Omnitrix symbol is still colored green.

===Ben 10,000 as Wildmutt===
[[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000's]] Wildmutt was larger than his 10-year-old self, had brown stripes on his back instead of apparent quills, he no longer has apparent quills in his arms, the apparent quills on his chin got bigger, his teeth are now larger, thicker and sharper, his appearance had shifted to a more feline form due to the presence of a tail. Wildmutt wore the [[Omnitrix (Original Future)|Omnitrix]] symbol on his forehead.

===Carl as Wildmutt===
[[Carl Tennyson|Carl]]'s Wildmutt looks the same as Ben's in '''''Destroy All Aliens''''', except he lacked the Omnitrix symbol.

