{{Quote|Good thinking. The Vulpin's keen senses should be able to sniff out the intruder.|[[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]] to Wildmutt.<ref name="SOTO">'''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]'''''</ref>}}
More animal than humanoid, Wildmutt is a beastly alien with superhuman athletic ability<ref name="ATTW10"/> and heightened senses of smell, hearing and taste.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben10-Wildmutt.png]]|group = CN}} As a trade-off to not having proper vision, Wildmutt's amazing sense of smell makes up a dull 360 "radar" that he uses to "see",{{Refn|[[:File:Vulpin Dark Caves.png]]|group = pop-up}} making it nearly impossible for opponents to sneak up on him.<ref name="ATTW10" /> He can tell how old someone is just by smelling them.{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Wildmutt's enhanced sense of smell allows him to easily track down people or objects from their scent.<ref>[[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax Shard]]</ref><ref name="SOTO"/><ref name="PN775IM">''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]''</ref><ref name="BA">''[[Ben Again]]''</ref> With it, [[Kevin 11]] was able to track down [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]].{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin Find Ben.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="BWaV">''[[Back With a Vengeance]]''</ref> His sense of smell also renders any kind of visual deception useless, as he can effortlessly identify and track entities that are invisible<ref name="FaTM">''[[Fight at the Museum]]''</ref> or wearing a disguise.<ref name="SZTWC">''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]''</ref>

Wildmutt possesses sharp teeth and an enhanced bite force, being able to rip wires and pieces out of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s [[Mechadroid|Mechadroids]];<ref name="ATTW10" /> harm a [[Limax]]<ref name="PR"/> and [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Animo]]'s [[Mutant Prairie Dog]];<ref name="N10P2">[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 2]]</ref> rip out a piece of the [[Rustbucket 3]];<ref name="TFOC">[[The Forge of Creation]]</ref> rip off wires ensnaring two [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumbers]]; <ref name="EE">[[Evil's Encore]]</ref> and chew through a telephone pole in seconds.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Wildmutt possesses sharp claws, being able to effortlessly slash through [[Cooper (Classic)|Cooper]]'s security drones;<ref name="N10P2" /> keep himself attached to a wall within the [[Resolute (Classic)|Resolute]] while the airlock was open;<ref name="SOTO"/> and quickly dig through stone.<ref name="BA" /> Additionally, Wildmutt's claws help him scale surfaces.<ref name="BWaV"/> His back claws are larger and more powerful than his front claws.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Wildmutt has enhanced strength, being able throw a dumpster at a group of Limax and tackle one of them into a wall;<ref name="PR"/> and tear off the roof of a car and fight off the [[Circus Freaks (Classic)|Circus Freaks]];<ref name="Last Laugh"/> carry a [[Florauna (Classic)|Florauna]] on his back while running without difficulty;<ref name="DFY">''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]''</ref> hold his own against a [[Buglizard]];<ref name="OPaPP1">''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]''</ref> and pin down a [[Merlinisapien]].<ref name="FaTM"/>

Wildmutt has enhanced durability, being able to jump through a window;<ref name="FaTM" /> take punches from a Limax;<ref name="PR"/> and survive a steel tower falling on top of him.<ref name="Last Laugh">''[[Last Laugh]]''</ref> Wildmutt is also very quick and agile,<ref name="DFY" /> being able to run faster than a cheetah.{{Refn|[[:File:Vulpimancers Faster Than Cheetahs.png]]|group = DR}} Additionally, he also has enhanced reflexes, being able to quickly dodge a sword slash from Eon<ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref> and trip a [[Kineceleran (Classic)|Kineceleran]] running at him.<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref>

Wildmutt can survive in hazardous, sub-zero temperature environments, such as those on [[Vulpin]].{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Bandai Card.png]]|group = Bandai}}{{Refn|Vulpin Plumber Database; files [[:File:WildmuttToxinImmunity1.png|1]], [[:File:WildmuttToxinImmunity2.png|2]]|group = VA|name = PD}} This allows Wildmutt to break through ice easily if frozen solid, as demonstrated by other Vulpimancers in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]].<ref name="SH">''[[Singlehanded]]''</ref>

Wildmutt is a quadruped. However, he is capable of standing on his hind legs.<ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref> In addition, his front feet are prehensile, as he is able to use them to reach out and grab objects much like a hand.

Wildmutt can fire the quills from his back as projectiles. However, he can only do this when he reaches adulthood.{{Refn|[[:File:The Visitor Pop-up (2).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="TV">''[[The Visitor]]''</ref>

Even though he may not seem like it, he is extremely intelligent.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

