==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
DepreyPresa1P88.png|Sensitive Hearing
Side (464).png|Blocked Vision (via Cold Virus)
</gallery>
When [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] becomes Wildmutt, he has no way of communicating verbally as he can only growl and snarl. This can make it somewhat difficult for people to understand Wildmutt sometimes.{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Cereal Card.png]]|group = CN}}{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Top Trumps Card.png]]|group = TT}}

Wildmutt's higher hearing range can be taken advantage of, as high frequency noises like a [[Sonic Pitch Whistle]]<ref name="Truth" /> or a [[Zaroffian|Zaroffian's]] whistle<ref name="OPaPP1" /> can overwhelm his senses and stun him. Wildmutt is also sensitive to strong smells.{{Refn|[[:File:Wildmutt Smells 1.png]]|group = ab}}{{Refn|''Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Extreme Alien Action!'', [[:File:Wildmutt Smells 2.png|Page 54]]|group = ab}}

Wildmutt is implied to be vulnerable to fire, as shown with some other Vulpimancers when they were repelled by [[Swampfire]]'s flames.<ref name="SH" />

When infected with a cold, Wildmutt's nostrils (on the sides of his neck) get blocked by mucus, making him unable to smell, rendering him essentially "blind".<ref>''[[Side Effects]]''</ref>

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Wildmutt first appeared in ''[[And Then There Were 10]]'', where he defeated one of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax's]] [[Mechadroid|Mechadroids]].
*In ''[[Permanent Retirement]]'', Wildmutt and [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] escaped from a group of [[Limax]] before they defeated one that was impersonating [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and followed the scent of the Limax ship to find it.
*In ''[[Last Laugh]]'', Wildmutt battled the [[Circus Freaks (Classic)|Circus Freaks]], but was scared into defeat by [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]].
*In ''[[Lucky Girl (Episode)|Lucky Girl]]'', Wildmutt tried to save some construction workers from falling, but Lucky Girl ended up doing so instead.
*In ''[[Side Effects]]'', Wildmutt, due to a cold, was unable to battle [[Clancy]] and ended up accidentally destroying things, including a market, and almost got Gwen blown up by fireworks.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Wildmutt briefly appeared while he was captured. Later, Wildmutt surrendered to Vilgax so the latter would spare Max and Gwen.
**Also, Wildmutt appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[Truth]]'', Wildmutt tried to negotiate by talking with two [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancer]]s, but failed and was forced to fight them.
*In ''[[The Big Tick]]'', Wildmutt failed to defeat the [[Great One]].
*In ''[[Framed]]'', Gwen mentioned Wildmutt was used by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] to terrorize Tallahassee, Florida. Later, Ben as Wildmutt was defeated by Kevin as [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]] and saved a cable car from falling into the sea.
*In ''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]'', Wildmutt tried to help a kid down from a tree only to be tricked and tortured by [[Ghostfreak]] in a dream.
*In ''[[Camp Fear]]'', Wildmutt searched for Max, during which he discovered the lower parts of [[Camp Opinicon]] and the sentient plants.
*In ''[[Tough Luck]]'', Wildmutt was used in a magic act and battled [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]] and [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] when they invaded the magic show.
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Wildmutt appeared three times. Firstly, he was used by the Master Control and accidentally scared a man in the process, causing him to fall off the boat and prompting Wildmutt to switch into [[Ripjaws (Classic)|Ripjaws]] to save him. Then, Wildmutt was seen in a photo. Later, in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]], Wildmutt tried to avoid Vilgax and [[Kevin 11]], but was caught and had to switch into [[Stinkfly (Classic)|Stinkfly]].
*In ''[[Midnight Madness]]'', Wildmutt tried to stop some thieves before being chased by the police.
*In ''[[Merry Christmas]]'', Wildmutt pretended to be a reindeer in order to get Gwen and [[Elsgood]] into [[Thomas Jingles|Mr. Jingles]]' factory.
*In ''[[Under Wraps]]'', Wildmutt hoed a field.
*In ''[[The Visitor]]'', Wildmutt stole Gwen's kite, prompting her to put him under a [[Spells (Classic)|spell]] that made several dogs fall in love with him. Wildmutt escaped them by hiding in a tree.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''', Wildmutt appeared when the Omnitrix malfunctioned. Later, Wildmutt helped [[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]] search for an intruder, who turned out to be Gwen. He then accidentally opened the air lock and saved Gwen from being sucked into space.
*In ''[[Don't Drink the Water]]'', four-year-old Wildmutt (Wildpup) defeated Hex's digger monster.
*In ''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 2]]'', Wildmutt battled the [[Mutant Prairie Dog]] and [[Cooper (Classic)|Cooper]]'s security drones.
*In ''[[Dogged Pursuit]]'', Wildmutt saved an old lady's purse and got complimented by her.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''', Wildmutt attacked Ben in a dream.
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Wildmutt was seen on TV.
*In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', Wildmutt tried to get the [[Rustbucket 3]] free before 16-year-old Ben reverted him.

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse===
*In ''[[Evil's Encore]]'', Wildmutt freed himself, Max, and Gwen from a sack.

===Alien Force=== 
*Wildmutt was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]'', Wildmutt was re-unlocked by the Master Control.{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DM}}

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]'', Wildmutt briefly appeared when [[King Xarion]] was searching through the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] for [[Ampfibian (Classic)|Ampfibian]].
*In ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'', Wildmutt was used off-screen to find [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]].
*In ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', Wildmutt searched for [[Prisoner 775]] and briefly battled him before going [[Ultimate Wildmutt|Ultimate]].
*In ''[[The Purge]]'', Wildmutt searched a [[Forever Knights|Forever Knight]] castle, but found nothing of importance.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Wildmutt appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', the Ultimatrix turned Kevin into Wildmutt during a car ride to the [[Techadon Factory]], which caused him to crash [[Kevin's Car (Original)|his car]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]'', Wildmutt went Ultimate to battle the [[Esoterica]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Wildmutt chased the [[Screegit]] while giving [[Pax]] a lift before he reverted.
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]'', Wildmutt fought [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]]. Later, Wildmutt tested some of [[Pakmar|Pakmar's]] dog whistles.
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', Wildmutt was dunked in the Ben 10 Dunk Tank.
*In ''[[Store 23]]'', Wildmutt was one of several aliens [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was showcasing for [[Ben 23]].
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', Wildmutt was used by 11-year-old Ben in 16-year-old Ben's body to track a pipe with coordinates.
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Wildmutt battled [[Twin Knights]] while trying to destroy the [[Highbreed Pulse Generator]] and defeated them.
*In ''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]'', Wildmutt sniffed [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]] and found that he was actually [[Jerry]] dressed up as a decoy.
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', Wildmutt battled [[Eon]] before coming to [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben's]] defense.
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', No Watch Ben as Wildmutt defeated [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]] as [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]].
*In ''[[No Honor Among Bros]]'', Wildmutt tried to find [[Fistrick]] in his lair.
*In ''[[Fight at the Museum]]'', Wildmutt chased and caught [[Subdora]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Wildmutt appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', Wildmutt was defeated by [[Vilgax (Original Future)|Vilgax]], so he switched into [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].

===[[Race Against Time Timeline]]===
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]''''', Wildmutt defeated Eon by throwing him out of [[Race Against Time Timeline|the timeline]] and helped [[Gwen Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Gwen]] with her magic act.

