==Trivia== 
*Counting TV footage, Wildmutt is the first alien to appear in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.
*Wildmutt is [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben's]] only alien that is incapable of verbal speech, due to lacking the vocal anatomy to do so.{{Refn|[[:File:Vulpimancers Can't Speak English.png]]|group = DJW}} However, the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] appears to fix this problem with [[Ultimate Wildmutt]]. Interestingly, when [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] turned into Wildmutt in ''[[Inspector 13]]'', he was able to growl out a sentence.
*Wildmutt is the only alien featured in '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time|Race Against Time]]''''' to have his voice actor reprise his role from the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]'''.
*Wildmutt was originally planned to be one of the playable aliens in the ''[[Game Creator]]'', but was soon removed from the game when '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' aired.
*Wildmutt's name in the Croatian version of the cartoon, "Psina," means "Great Dog," but the same word is sometimes used to name several sharks, especially the [[Wikipedia:Great white shark|Great white shark]], which sometimes caused naming confusions between him and Ripjaws.
*Wildmutt's toys did not sell well.{{Refn|[[:File:Bipedal design reasons.PNG]]|group = STS}}
*Wildmutt served as a replacement for [[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)/Early Development#Digger|Digger]], an orange humanoid hero with digging abilities, when the crew decided to switch from superheroes to aliens. [[Dave Johnson]] designed him but noted that, like [[Ripjaws (Classic)|Ripjaws]] and [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]], it was hard for animators to draw him.{{Refn|https://archive.vn/VLRUq|group = DJ}}
*Had he appeared on-screen, [[Mad Ben]]'s Wildmutt would have some kind of harness and collar with spikes.{{Refn|[[:File:Mad Ben Wildmutt.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Had Wildmutt been featured in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]], he would have been more humanoid. The crew did not want him looking anything but a dog,{{Refn|[[:File:RB Wildmutt Would Have Been Humanoid.png]]|group = DR}} so he was not included in the show, even though [[Duncan Rouleau]] likes him.{{Refn|[[:File:RB No Wildmutt.png]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|https://youtu.be/IzdAJuPoKnU|group = DR}}
*Wildmutt is [[Joe Kelly]]'s and [[Robert Carey]]'s favorite alien.{{Refn|https://twitter.com/yasinemiralkaya/status/1771639134660055254|group = JK}}{{Refn|[[:File:Robert Carey is a Wildmutt fanboy.png]]|group = RC}}
*Because of how he does not see in the conventional sense, it's possible that Wildmutt cannot be scared by [[Toepick|Toepick's]] [[Toepick's Species|species]].{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Cannot Scare Vulpimancers.png]]|group = DJW}}

